+/* vroom: the frame's way through an IOSurface (vrend_shm_surface.h), for
+ * BGRA formats (what windows use): the surface, and a rectangle texture on
+ * it (CGL takes IOSurfaces as rectangle textures, and as BGRA only), so it
+ * holds what the CPU copy would.  Only for frames of 0.6 megapixels and up:
+ * Metal's round trip costs the GL thread 0.2 to 0.3 ms whatever the size,
+ * which is what the CPU copy of an 800x600 frame costs (2560x1600: 0.9 ms
+ * against 1.8, of which 0.3 on the CPU).  Without it (VROOM_SHM_COPY=1,
+ * another format, a smaller frame, no Metal), the CPU copy. */
